A teacher in the top quartile of effectiveness can produce an additional $400,000 in lifetime earnings per pupil compared to an average teacher — teacher quality is the most powerful in-school variable.
Districts that raised teacher pay competitively with local labour markets saw turnover fall by 8–12% and student test scores improve by 3–7 percentile points over 5 years.
Teach For America data shows that high-ability graduates are 60% more likely to persist in teaching if salary exceeds $60,000; below $45,000 the dropout rate accelerates sharply.
